      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **[[write-journal]]** page describes how the Guarded Write Journal works as part of Grimoire\u0027s write safety mechanism. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function:** Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it journals that file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content if it existed, or records that it didn\u0027t exist. This information is kept in an in-memory journal.\n\n**Rollback capability:** If the agent run fails (whether from hitting a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or rejected writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order. Files that existed are restored to their previous content, and newly created files are deleted.\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics:** This approach provides atomicity for all writes in a single run without requiring a database transaction\u2014the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held in the process\u0027s memory for that run\u0027s duration.\n\n**Note on Query agents:** The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write tool at all, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
